frame:
A finished trading-card frame template for a science-fiction board game about building artificial intelligence, seen flat-on, filling the whole image edge to edge, portrait shape exactly 69:94 (a little wider than 2:3). The attached picture is a layout guide, not a style reference: match its zone positions and sizes exactly, and paint over its flat color blocks.

Color key of the guide: the saturated color is the frame body and the header strip across the top, both in the card kind's color; the outside gray is a thin outer edge, which runs off every edge of the image. In the header strip, at the far left, is one red octagon: a socket for a cost. The rest of the strip is plain and uninterrupted. The pink band below it is the name banner. The guide's red, pink and cream are only markers, never colors to paint: the octagon's inside and the banner are ivory, or a very pale tint of the kind color. The large white area is the art window.{top} The cream area under it is the effect panel, a text area.

These are the ONLY elements. Paint the octagon as one empty physical socket, and the banner and panels as empty plates, exactly in those places. Empty means empty. Do not add any other socket, plate, circle, tab, button, gauge or dial anywhere: the right-hand part of the header strip stays a smooth, unbroken band of the kind color, because other parts are printed onto it later.

The kind color is the point of this frame. {kind} It must be bright, lit and saturated, the way the bold colored frames of a modern hobby board game are: a large, confident, glowing area of color you notice from across a table, not a tinted rim on a dark or gray frame. The whole picture is high-key and brightly lit, with no heavy black areas, no gloom and no vignette.

Hard rules:
- absolutely no text, letters, numbers, glyphs, symbols, logos or icons anywhere, not even fake or decorative ones;
- the art window is one plain, flat, even pale gray rectangle with no texture, gradient, picture or pattern, because card art fills it later;
- light mode: the effect panel, name banner and the inside of the octagon are light, smooth and quiet, so that dark text printed on them would read easily;
- keep the frame's detail in the band and the strip, not over the text areas;
- do not draw a card lying on a surface, a shadow around the card, a border outside the frame or a mockup: the frame IS the image.

