containers:
A flat product sheet of six separate empty game-piece containers, in exactly the finish of the attached card frame: bright polished brushed steel bevels with fine scuffs and crisp specular highlights, thick glossy enamel. Seen dead flat-on, no perspective. The background is one perfectly flat, uniform pure magenta (#ff00ff) with no shadow, gradient or glow, and nothing touches it except the six objects. Six objects in two rows of three, evenly spaced, none touching, each about a quarter of the image wide or less.

Top row, left to right:
1. a square tile with slightly rounded corners: a slim steel bevel around a flat pale gray enamel face;
2. a round disc: a slim steel rim around a flat pale gray enamel face, like a thick token;
3. a ring: a slim round steel rim around a flat very dark charcoal enamel face.

Bottom row, left to right:
4. a wide rounded rectangle, 3:1, a slim dark steel bevel around flat warm brown enamel: an income box;
5. a wide rectangle, 3:1, with cut corners, a heavy black gunmetal bevel with sharp edges around a flat near-black face: an ominous frame;
6. a round steel-rimmed disc with a flat ivory face, the same size as object 2.

Hard rules: every face is flat, plain and empty; absolutely no text, letters, numbers, glyphs, symbols, logos, icons or patterns anywhere; no drop shadows; no magenta anywhere on the objects.
